-- diveday:allow-destructive drop-table roll_call_crew_attestations: retired by H-46 (ADR 20260804-crew-roll-call-is-per-person superseding 20260802-crew-roll-call-attestation) - the per-person crew roll call is the whole crew half of a head count. The table has no writer at all: recordCrewAttestation's only callers were its own tests, nothing seeds it, and it is empty in every environment. This is NOT expand/contract-clean, and saying so plainly: the *previous* release still SELECTs it in three places this same change removes - the export bundle, that bundle's row-count query behind Settings, and the owner-only departure log - so for the length of the production build window those surfaces raise 42P01 and 500. No data is lost (there is none) and no writer breaks. Accepted under H-49: pre-pilot, no users, no data worth retaining.
DROP TABLE "roll_call_crew_attestations";
